# Lab 04 — Azure RBAC Troubleshooting

## Objective

Investigate a scenario where authentication succeeds but Azure authorization does not provide the required access.

This lab demonstrates an evidence-based troubleshooting workflow:

```text
Authentication
      ↓
Success
      ↓
Resource access attempted
      ↓
Authorization evaluation
      ↓
Access problem
      ↓
Role assignment investigation
      ↓
Scope / inheritance / group investigation
      ↓
Root cause
      ↓
Least-privilege remediation
      ↓
Validation
```

---

## Learning Objectives

By the end of this lab, I will be able to:

- Distinguish authentication failure from authorization failure.
- Investigate Azure RBAC assignments.
- Investigate scope and inheritance.
- Investigate group-based access.
- Identify missing or excessive permissions.
- Use Azure Activity Log during authorization investigations.
- Apply a least-privilege remediation.
- Validate the final result.

---

## 1. Troubleshooting Scenario

The lab will use an actual OsCorp identity and Azure resource scenario.

Do not invent the failure.

Complete the scenario details after the access test has been performed.

